    "description": "For the whole run, 30% of the first model's streams end without warning at a random 20 to 80% of the answer, after the client has started reading it. Switchyard should finish each one on the second model in the same stream (mid-stream failover, spec 7.6). Every request streams, since only streamed answers are continued; a cut non-streamed answer is an ordinary failover. 30% stays under the breaker's 40% rule, so most requests still reach the primary and hundreds of them are continued; a run of 5 cuts in a row can still open the breaker for a while.",
